# ForkIt — AI Rules

## Project
ForkIt is a social-first food discovery app for Malaysia. React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + Supabase + Framer Motion. Web-first MVP, React Native later.

## Stack
- Frontend: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Framer Motion, React Router v6
- State: Zustand (global), React hooks (local)
- Backend: Supabase (Auth, PostgreSQL, Realtime, Storage, Edge Functions)
- AI: Gemini 1.5 Flash via lib/ai.ts abstraction layer
- Maps: Google Maps JS API via lib/maps.ts
- Places: Google Places API via lib/places.ts
- Push: Web Push API + VAPID keys via lib/push.ts
- Hosting: Vercel

## Folder rules
- features/x/ owns its own components, hooks, local state
- features/ never imports from other features/
- Cross-feature communication via Zustand store or URL params only
- Shared UI goes in components/
- All external API calls go through lib/ wrappers — never call APIs directly from components
- Always import supabase from @/lib/supabase — never instantiate a new client

## Code style
- TypeScript strict mode — no any unless absolutely necessary
- Functional components only — no class components
- Tailwind for all styling — no inline style objects except Framer Motion animations
- All types defined in types/index.ts or co-located in the feature
- Path alias: @/ maps to src/

## Brand
- Primary accent: #FF4D00 (orange-red)
- Secondary accent: #FF0080 (pink)
- Success: #00A86B (green)
- Dark bg: #0F0E0C, Surface: #161513
- Light bg: #FAF7F2
- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans (headings, 700/800), Inter (body, 400-700)

## DB schema (Phase 1 tables)
- users: id, display_name, avatar_url, bio, personality_type, budget_pref, distance_pref
- user_preferences: user_id, cuisine_tags[], dietary_tags[], notification_prefs jsonb
- restaurants: id, google_place_id, name, cuisine, lat, lng, price_range, rating, photos[]
- saved_places: user_id, restaurant_id, geofence_active, last_notified_at, visit_count
- reviews: id, user_id, restaurant_id, rating, body

## Key patterns
- Supabase client: import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase'
- AI calls: import { askAI } from '@/lib/ai' — never call Gemini directly
- Auth state: import { useUserStore } from '@/store/userStore'
- When in doubt, check the feature folder first before creating a new shared component
